From 90ac304ad9bd35a616a486f86775ca43680b9bcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DByte308 <69403407+DByte308@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:36:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] d/pimax_p3c: check the refresh rate against the headset's
 stored EDID

A requested PIMAX_REFRESH_HZ is only sent when the headset's display lists
that rate in its EDID. But the display only comes up about a second after
the rate is sent and video is started, so the EDID was never there in
time: every session fell back to the model default, whatever was chosen.

Once video has started, wait for the display in the background and store
its EDID per headset serial in the config directory. Later sessions check
the requested rate against that copy (or the live EDID, if the display is
already up), so a rate the panel cannot drive still never reaches it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
